WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
Secure the paper. Support the forearm as needed.
Choose a comfortable pen or assessed grip aid.

00:06.000 --> 00:12.000
A short pattern is shown with a thick-grip pen.
Your grasp and marks may look different.

00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
Relax the hand. No standard grip is required.
Move the paper closer instead of overreaching.

00:18.000 --> 00:24.000
Example replay: short, easy strokes.
Do not force finger or wrist range.

00:24.000 --> 00:30.000
Rest. Ask an OT about useful adaptations.
Typing or dictation can help with longer text.

00:30.000 --> 00:36.000
A final example, at your chosen pace.
One comfortable mark is enough.

00:36.000 --> 00:42.000
Writing is expression, not a clinical test.
Record comfort or difficulty if you wish.
